WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.880
In one cross-test, the Foundation thought&nbsp;
SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy Reptile, would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.720
bite off more than it could chew with SCP-807,&nbsp;
a deadly plate from the Last Chance Diner.

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.120
This plate makes any food placed on it&nbsp;
extra delicious, but also makes them extra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:20.080
unhealthy - so unhealthy that people who eat&nbsp;
its food tend to die of massive heart attacks.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:25.360
They used the plate to transmute two&nbsp;
SCP-682 Specials - a mix of 10 kg of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:31.280
rotten meat and sharpened bone splinters, 10&nbsp;
L of rancid mayonnaise, 1 L potassium cyanide,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:35.840
and 1 kg morphine hydrochloride -&nbsp;
considered a 5-star course for our pal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.800
SCP-682 - and fed it to the beast.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.600
At first, it seemed immobile. Perhaps the&nbsp;
monster had been bested? But when D-Classes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:46.960
entered to check, the creature’s&nbsp;
skin ruptured in several areas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:50.320
ejecting high-pressure jets of&nbsp;
its own blood in every direction,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:57.280
killing them all. The reptile was completely fine&nbsp;
afterward and eagerly ate a third 682 Special.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:02.800
In one cross-test, the Hard to Destroy&nbsp;
Reptile SCP-682 was made to face off against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:06.560
SCP-689, the terrifying Haunter in the Dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:11.440
a statue that can induce death in anyone who&nbsp;
looks at it and then stops paying attention.

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:16.320
The statue was placed in 682’s chamber, and&nbsp;
the lights were turned off for five minutes.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.280
When the lights were turned back on, 682&nbsp;
laid motionless in a pile of dark, grey goo.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:26.560
When a D-Class was sent in to confirm the kill,&nbsp;
682 suddenly rose back up to its feet and devoured&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:32.240
him in an instant. Two swift chomps with its&nbsp;
razor sharp teeth, and the D-Class was history.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:36.640
It seems that 682 doesn’t fit the same&nbsp;
definition of “alive” as us humans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:42.000
and, as a result, was unaffected by the Haunter&nbsp;
in the Dark. Frighteningly, 682 was also smart&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:48.640
enough to intuit 689’s anomalous ability and used&nbsp;
this knowledge to play dead and attempt escape.

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:55.520
It’s the clash of the titans: SCP-682,&nbsp;
the Hard to Destroy Reptile, vs SCP-096,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.520 --> 00:01:59.040
the terrifying, murderous Shy&nbsp;
Guy. But who won this battle?

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:03.520
Well...It was kind of a draw. Their&nbsp;
battle lasted for 27 whole hours,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.240
and ended in a brutal stalemate, with&nbsp;
SCP-096 severely injured and huddled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.240 --> 00:02:14.240
in one corner of the room, and 682 in the&nbsp;
other, missing 85% of its original body mass.

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.600
The creatures were both brought back&nbsp;
to their chambers with relative ease.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:24.320
A fight like this can never happen again, because&nbsp;
now, whenever 096 is brought too close to 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.880
it turns away, shrieks, and&nbsp;
begins clawing at its own face.

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:35.840
In one cross test, SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy
Reptile, was made to face off against SCP-1361,

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:41.360
a giant, aggressive mass of animal slurry
that envelops and digests everything it touches,

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.920
before briefly taking on their traits.

00:02:43.920 --> 00:02:51.280
Just over 1000 kilograms of SCP-1361 was poured
onto SCP-682, and it successfully enveloped

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.080
the creature.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:56.400
The problem was that it then began taking
on traits and a temperament incredibly similar

00:02:56.400 --> 00:03:02.800
to SCP-682 - After developing legs, jaws and
other physical features similar to the reptile,

00:03:02.800 --> 00:03:06.400
it broke out of containment and killed seventeen
members of staff.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:10.480
After several failed attempts to stop the
creature with small arms fire, it was finally

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:13.200
destroyed by the aerial deployment of napalm.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.920
682’s skeletal carcass was retrieved from
within and placed back in its chamber.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:22.800
It had regenerated back to perfect health
within a mere six hours.

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:27.200
We all have that one friend, we just can’t
take anywhere with us without a little explanation

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.880
and a whole lot of embarrassment.

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:34.222
Nobody expected what would happen when the
SCP Foundation cross-tested SCP-682, the Hard

00:03:34.222 --> 00:03:40.000
to Destroy Reptile, with SCP-082, a giant,
aggressive humanoid called Fernand the Cannibal.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.720
When they presented Fernand with a tissue
sample of 682, he said, “Oh, splendid!

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:46.240
My friend lives!”

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:50.320
When he entered the containment chamber, 682
immediately attempted to flee from him, despite

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:55.440
Fernand claiming they were friends who went
way back - And, in fact, 682 had once been

00:03:55.440 --> 00:03:56.800
his loyal steed.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:04:01.440
After extended fighting, Fernand began to
ride 682, an experience the reptile found

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.960
supremely humiliating.

00:04:02.960 --> 00:04:08.720
Once 082 left, the giant was delighted, and
SCP-682 said something about him that we can’t

00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.920
repeat if we want to keep monetization on
this video.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:17.600
In one particularly exciting cross test, the
Foundation set SCP-682, the infamous Hard

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:23.280
to Destroy Reptile, against SCP-204, a cloud
of deadly, all-consuming nanites bonded to

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:26.000
a small child for the purposes of protecting
them.

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:31.280
As SCP-682 naturally attacked the child, the
nanites sprung into action, forming the shape

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.680
of a huge warrior with an axe and shield.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:39.120
The battle was intense, but amazingly, despite
taking tremendous damage itself, the SCP-204

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:42.160
warrior kicked the stuffing out of SCP-682.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:48.400
As is expected of SCP-204, its nanites began
feeding on SCP-682’s immobilized body.

00:04:48.400 --> 00:04:51.920
But, surprise surprise,&nbsp;
SCP-682 started regenerating&nbsp;

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:53.680
faster than the nanites could eat it.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.120
It then began to attack SCP-204 once again.

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:02.080
The Foundation tranquilized both parties,
and hosed SCP-682 with hydrochloric acid,

00:05:02.080 --> 00:05:04.240
before returning them both to their chambers.

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:05.920
All anomalies contained.

00:05:05.920 --> 00:05:07.520
No children harmed.

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:11.520
Delegating a high-priority task to a person
who only delivers a bare-minimum style of

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:15.440
work ethic otherwise, will probably result
in the task not getting done.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:21.600
The Foundation tried to snuff out SCP-682
with the help of SCP-2599, formerly known

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:27.040
as Zena Cho, a woman of Korean descent who’ll
carry out any order you give her...But only

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:28.240
around halfway.

00:05:28.240 --> 00:05:33.600
That’s why the Foundation ordered her to
attack 682 until it was “200% dead”, so

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:38.400
even if she only did her task by halves, it’d
still be 100% dead.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.840
By all accounts, she was actually doing a
pretty solid job, horrifically mutilating

00:05:41.840 --> 00:05:46.080
the creature to a point of near-death, when
it suddenly yelled “KILL ME, YOU SACK OF

00:05:46.080 --> 00:05:47.760
ORGANS, DO IT!”

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:51.920
And that order seemingly confused her, seeing
as only going halfway on killing the creature

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:53.680
was something she’d already done.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:57.280
She remained motionless in the test chamber
until she was physically removed, and later

00:05:57.280 --> 00:06:01.200
attempts to use her in 682’s termination
were fruitless.

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:07.360
The Foundation once tried to kill SCP-682,
the Hard to Destroy Reptile, with SCP-272,

00:06:07.360 --> 00:06:08.720
an old iron nail.

00:06:08.720 --> 00:06:13.200
This anomalous nail can kill its victims in
a number of ways: The nail bind’s a victim’s

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:17.360
shadow to the ground, indirectly binding the
victim itself as well by doing so.

00:06:17.360 --> 00:06:21.920
If the shadow is displaced due to changes
in light source, the victim is flung and contorted

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.160
in the same direction the shadow has moved.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.840
If the victim tries to destroy the nail, they
will surely die.

00:06:27.840 --> 00:06:32.400
After the Foundation intentionally made the
lights in 682’s chamber strobe on and off

00:06:32.400 --> 00:06:36.320
from various directions, causing the reptile
to be mutilated by being hurled around the

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:36.640
room.

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.680
Its body began producing an extremely powerful
light source, eliminating its own shadow and

00:06:41.680 --> 00:06:42.880
keeping it safe.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.120
The light was so bright that when D-Classes
entered the chamber to remove the nail - despite

00:06:47.120 --> 00:06:50.800
wearing eye protection - they were afflicted
with permanent retinal damage.

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.280
And of course - in the end - SCP-682 was just
fine.

00:06:55.280 --> 00:07:00.080
In one of their more desperate attempts to&nbsp;
kill off SCP-682, the Hard to Destroy Reptile,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:04.160
the SCP Foundation employed the use of SCP-3802,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.160 --> 00:07:08.240
a bottle of anti-baldness ointment&nbsp;
known as “hare growth by dado.”

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:11.920
But not just any hair: If you&nbsp;
apply this to the skin of an adult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:15.680
they’ll break out in huge, painful,&nbsp;
tumorous masses that turn into giant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:15.680 --> 00:07:21.280
Flemish rabbits. This anomalous chemical&nbsp;
was spritzed onto SCP-682 by the sprinklers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.280 --> 00:07:25.040
causing the beast horrific pain and&nbsp;
massive, unchecked tumor growth.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:28.560
As these tumors broke away and became&nbsp;
giant rabbits, they tore off 40%&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.480
of SCP-682’s body mass. However, it didn’t stick,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.480 --> 00:07:37.840
as SCP-682 ate the rabbits while it was&nbsp;
regenerating. Back to the drawing board!

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:43.200
Who would win: The Hard to Destroy Reptile,
or 9.15 million kilograms of bananas?

00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:47.520
This is SCP-682 VS SCP-3521

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:53.280
When SCP-682 was cross-tested with SCP-3521
- A little yellow pill that makes bananas

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:57.680
manifest in the stomach of those who eat them
- the Foundation hoped to answer that question.

00:07:57.680 --> 00:08:02.000
682 was tricked into eating the pill by hiding
it inside the body of a dead cow, which was

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.360
then fed to the monster.

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:09.040
As time passed, an absurd number of bananas
began to manifest in and around SCP-682, filling

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:11.600
its containment chamber and then the entire
facility.

00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:15.840
However, just when it seemed 682 was crushed
under all that potassium, it began eating

00:08:15.840 --> 00:08:18.160
the bananas faster than they could be produced.

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:23.200
And because bananas are each slightly naturally
radioactive, eating that many gave SCP-682

00:08:23.200 --> 00:08:28.320
the ability to fire a powerful radiation beam
out of its mouth until 3521’s effects wore

00:08:28.320 --> 00:08:28.640
off.

00:08:28.640 --> 00:08:29.680
The craziest part?

00:08:29.680 --> 00:08:32.000
This all occurred within a ten-minute period.

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.720
Guess you could say things went a little bananas
in there.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.760
Ready for this one?

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:43.360
SCP-682 vs SCP-835 is one of the most horrifying
SCP-682 cross tests we have logged to date!

00:08:43.360 --> 00:08:44.080
That’s right!

00:08:44.080 --> 00:08:49.680
We have paired the Hard to Destroy Reptile
with the disgusting nightmare known as SCP-835,

00:08:49.680 --> 00:08:53.360
a giant carnivorous coral polyp made from
living human matter!

00:08:53.360 --> 00:08:59.280
When SCP-835 was released, the infectious
abomination pulled SCP-682 into its massive

00:08:59.280 --> 00:09:04.160
gullet, dragging it down for a slow and painful
digestion, surrounded by the intense pressure

00:09:04.160 --> 00:09:07.200
and screaming human faces of the beast’s
fleshy throat.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:10.720
What was eventually ejected was little more
than SCP-682’s skeleton.

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:18.000
However, over time this skeleton regenerated
into a horrific hybrid of SCP-682 and SCP-835:

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:22.720
Covered in sticky tentacles, human faces spewing
acid, and infectious spores that could turn

00:09:22.720 --> 00:09:24.320
others into monsters.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:26.320
It breached containment and killed many.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:31.760
The survivors had to be terminated to avoid
SCP-835 contamination spreading further.

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:37.520
SCP-682 Vs Godzilla: Who would take home the
gold in the battle of these mighty reptiles?

00:09:37.520 --> 00:09:42.080
Godzilla, obviously, has the advantage in
terms of his offensive capabilities: He’s

00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:47.280
considerably larger than SCP-682, and has
the incredible power of his atomic breath

00:09:47.280 --> 00:09:52.480
- Capable of taking down other huge monsters
like King Ghidorah or the MUTOs.

00:09:52.480 --> 00:09:57.360
However, SCP-682 has its trump card: Insane
adaptability.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:10:01.440
When faced with Godzilla, it may adapt to
imitate the monster’s atomic breath, or

00:10:01.440 --> 00:10:04.720
begin to grow to epic proportions to match
it in size.

00:10:04.720 --> 00:10:08.880
In the end, it’s hard to know who would
win, but a true stalemate seems incredibly

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:09.600
likely.

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:16.400
It’s time for a clash of the titans: SCP-682, the&nbsp;
Hard to Destroy Reptile, SCP-106, the Old Man,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.400 --> 00:10:21.840
and SCP-953, the Polymorphic Humanoid.&nbsp;
This wasn’t even a Foundation cross-test:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:25.520
Just an organic battle that occurred&nbsp;
during a massive containment breach.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:32.240
SCP-953 and SCP-106 entered 682’s containment&nbsp;
chamber, at which point they all began staring at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:38.000
each other, preparing for an attack. 106 began the&nbsp;
battle, sinking into the floor and grabbing 953,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.760
trying to pull her into his pocket&nbsp;
dimension. She then grabbed 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:45.040
resulting in all three of them being&nbsp;
pulled into the pocket dimension.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.520
They all remained in there for five hours, before&nbsp;
returning, heavily injured from their fight.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.520 --> 00:10:55.840
106 returned to his chamber, 953 was recaptured&nbsp;
by Foundation personnel, and 682 regenerated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:55.840 --> 00:11:01.600
its 67% body mass loss. All three have&nbsp;
refused to speak about the incident since.

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:08.240
The cross-test between SCP-682 and SCP-173 with&nbsp;
high precision blades was a complete disaster.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:12.320
Organized by Dr. Shenron, the two iconic&nbsp;
monsters were brought into a test chamber&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:15.440
and the blades were deployed,&nbsp;
cutting both of them into pieces.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:20.480
Two D-Classes were sent in when the vacuum&nbsp;
system failed, and were killed by SCP-682’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:20.480 --> 00:11:25.760
blobs of flesh, and the newly reformed&nbsp;
SCP-173. At this point, the battle began,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:30.400
and 173 attacked the different blobs&nbsp;
of 682 flesh. Some blobs fought back,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:35.200
while others reformed into a smaller&nbsp;
version of 682, which stared at 173.

00:11:35.200 --> 00:11:39.440
Just like in the original test, a sniper&nbsp;
shot out the eyes of this smaller 682,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.440 --> 00:11:44.000
leading 173 to snap its neck. It then&nbsp;
regenerated and stared at 173 for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:48.800
seventeen hours before the test was finally&nbsp;
ended. When 173 was taken back to its cell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:53.680
there was a power failure in the hallway, leading&nbsp;
to a site-wide containment breach and many deaths.

00:11:53.680 --> 00:11:54.067
Dr. Shenron’s troubleshooting with&nbsp;
the incinerator system was seen as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.067 --> 00:11:54.160
the catalyst for this deadly power failure, and&nbsp;
he was relieved from duty shortly afterwards.

00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:58.160
SCP-682 Vs The Gate Guardian.&nbsp;
Can the giant warrior with a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:01.520
sword hotter than the sun finally&nbsp;
kill the Hard to Destroy Reptile?

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:06.160
When SCP-682 was brought in to hopefully&nbsp;
meet its ultimate destruction at the Gate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.840
the Guardian Guards, it quipped,&nbsp;
“Is this meant to be the Garden?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:15.440
This is not the Garden. The&nbsp;
Garden is far west of here.”

00:12:15.440 --> 00:12:20.480
When the Gate Guardian struck 682, it was&nbsp;
grievously wounded, with only a single leg left.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.480 --> 00:12:25.440
As it regenerated, it snarled at the Gate&nbsp;
Guardian, saying, “Die? You command me&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:31.920
to die? Oh, wouldn't we all like that, but&nbsp;
this is my curse for suggesting the fruit.”&nbsp;

00:12:31.920 --> 00:12:35.680
It struck again, and before passing&nbsp;
out from its injuries, 682 said,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.720 --> 00:12:51.840
“This is not the Garden, and&nbsp;
you are not Uriel. Pretender.”

